# Attempt intake policy

What the coordinator does with an attempt a worker posts, decided from facts the
coordinator established itself — never from what the worker says it found.

The facts are checked in order of what is cheapest to fake. A worker whose lease
lapsed or was handed on (a stale fencing token) changes nothing. An attempt and a
trail entry that disagree with the unit about the problem change nothing. A trail
entry whose hash does not seal its own contents is refused. An approach already
recorded as a dead end on this problem is refused, so no contributor pays twice for
the same wall. Everything else is recorded, and three things follow from it:

- an entry written against an older head of the trail is RESEALED onto the head (a
  concurrent attempt got there first; the content is unchanged, its place moves);
- a failed approach is recorded as a dead end;
- a claimed proof becomes a `verify` unit for the trusted verifier. A worker's
  verdict is a claim. The coordinator marks nothing proved on it; only an
  attestation does, and the schema refuses a solved node without one.

## A IntakeFacts has:
    a leaseLive, which is Bool.
    a sameProblem, which is Bool.
    an entrySealed, which is Bool.
    an atHead, which is Bool.
    a deadEnd, which is Bool.
    a claimedVerified, which is Bool.
    a failedApproach, which is Bool.

## A IntakeDecision has:
    an accept, which is Bool.
    a status, which is Int.
    an outcome, which is Text.
    a reseal, which is Bool.
    a recordDeadEnd, which is Bool.
    an enqueueVerify, which is Bool.

## Note
A refusal: nothing is written.

## To refuseIntake (status: Int, outcome: Text) -> IntakeDecision:
    Return a new IntakeDecision with accept false and status status and outcome outcome and reseal false and recordDeadEnd false and enqueueVerify false.

## Note
The decision on one attempt.

## To decideIntake (f: IntakeFacts) -> IntakeDecision:
    If f's leaseLive is equal to false:
        Return refuseIntake(409, "stale_lease").
    If f's sameProblem is equal to false:
        Return refuseIntake(422, "mismatched_problem").
    If f's entrySealed is equal to false:
        Return refuseIntake(422, "unsealed_entry").
    If f's deadEnd:
        Return refuseIntake(409, "dead_end").
    Let mutable outcome be "recorded".
    If f's claimedVerified:
        Set outcome to "awaiting_verifier".
    Return a new IntakeDecision with accept true and status 201 and outcome outcome and reseal (f's atHead is equal to false) and recordDeadEnd f's failedApproach and enqueueVerify f's claimedVerified.

## Note
Every fact true but the ones named, for the tests.

## To factsWith (leaseLive: Bool, deadEnd: Bool, claimedVerified: Bool) -> IntakeFacts:
    Return a new IntakeFacts with leaseLive leaseLive and sameProblem true and entrySealed true and atHead true and deadEnd deadEnd and claimedVerified claimedVerified and failedApproach false.

## Test: intake records a clean attempt at the head

Let d be decideIntake(factsWith(true, false, false)).
Expect that d's accept is equal to true.
Expect that d's status is equal to 201.
Expect that d's outcome is equal to "recorded".
Expect that d's reseal is equal to false.
Expect that d's enqueueVerify is equal to false.

## Test: intake refuses stale leases, mismatches, unsealed entries and dead ends

Expect that decideIntake(factsWith(false, false, true))'s outcome is equal to "stale_lease".
Expect that decideIntake(factsWith(true, true, false))'s outcome is equal to "dead_end".
Expect that decideIntake(factsWith(true, true, false))'s status is equal to 409.
Let mutable f be factsWith(true, false, false).
Set f's sameProblem to false.
Expect that decideIntake(f)'s outcome is equal to "mismatched_problem".
Set f's sameProblem to true.
Set f's entrySealed to false.
Expect that decideIntake(f)'s status is equal to 422.

## Test: intake reseals an entry written against an older head

Let mutable f be factsWith(true, false, false).
Set f's atHead to false.
Set f's failedApproach to true.
Let d be decideIntake(f).
Expect that d's reseal is equal to true.
Expect that d's recordDeadEnd is equal to true.

## Test: intake never settles a claim and records only with a live lease

For all booleans live and sameProblem and sealed and head and dead and claimed and failed:
    Let f be a new IntakeFacts with leaseLive live and sameProblem sameProblem and entrySealed sealed and atHead head and deadEnd dead and claimedVerified claimed and failedApproach failed.
    Let d be decideIntake(f).
    Expect that d's accept is equal to (live and sameProblem and sealed and dead is equal to false).
    Expect that d's enqueueVerify is equal to (d's accept and claimed).
    Expect that d's outcome is not equal to "solved".
    Expect that (d's accept is equal to false and (d's reseal or d's recordDeadEnd)) is equal to false.
